---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import AuthorityPanel from '@/components/ia/AuthorityPanel.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="SPDTF 2.0 Working groups"
  description="The canonical SPDTF 2.0 working-group family: bounded-context groups, the DBT Smart Data scheme group and Interoperability."
>
  <PageMeta category="Working groups" variant="brand" updated="Participation and candidate review · 2026-08-18" />
  <h1>SPDTF 2.0 working groups</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Working groups are one canonical family inside SPDTF 2.0 Development. Practitioners
    contribute evidence, language, examples and judgement; facilitators make that
    meaning reviewable and machine-readable. Registration or a generated page does not
    confer membership, consensus or standards authority.
  </p>

  <AuthorityPanel destination="working-groups" />

  <h2 id="roster">The working-group family</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#finance" title="Finance and Banking" eyebrow="Bounded context" description="Mortgage journey, lending decisions, parties, evidence, risk and finance-data exchange." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#conveyancing" title="Conveyancing" eyebrow="Bounded context" description="Instruction, legal transfer, enquiries, searches, exchange and completion." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#estate-agency" title="Estate Agency" eyebrow="Bounded context" description="Marketing, listings, material information, viewings, offers and seller information." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#surveying" title="Surveying and Valuation" eyebrow="Bounded context" description="Inspection, condition, valuation, professional evidence and property risk." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#data-services" title="Property Data Services" eyebrow="Bounded context" description="Registries, searches, authoritative sources, provenance, currency and reuse." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#technology" title="Property Technology" eyebrow="Bounded context" description="Platforms, workflow, integration, APIs, implementation and operational feedback." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#dbt-smart-data" title="DBT Smart Data" eyebrow="OPDA-internal scheme group" description="Participants, roles, trust, consent, authorisation, accreditation, liability and cross-sector alignment." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups#interoperability" title="Interoperability Working Group" eyebrow="Peer cross-cutting group" description="The small common boundary, context map, cross-context mappings and shared exchange conventions." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="workspace">A common workspace shape</h2>
  <p>Each group works through the same review path, while retaining ownership of its local meaning:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>charter, scope, competency questions and decision owner;</li>
    <li>participation routes, evidence register and source handling;</li>
    <li>glossary, dictionary, taxonomies, controlled vocabularies, resources and relationships;</li>
    <li>candidate versions, open questions, feedback dispositions and change history;</li>
    <li>coverage assessment, technical views and generated exports.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="finance">Finance and Banking</h2>
  <h2 id="conveyancing">Conveyancing</h2>
  <h2 id="estate-agency">Estate Agency</h2>
  <h2 id="surveying">Surveying and Valuation</h2>
  <h2 id="data-services">Property Data Services</h2>
  <h2 id="technology">Property Technology</h2>
  <h2 id="dbt-smart-data">DBT Smart Data scheme group</h2>
  <p>
    This is an OPDA-internal cross-sector scheme-design group, not a government-established
    property scheme body. Its name and work cannot confer statutory or government-approved
    status on SPDTF. It supplies scheme-level questions and requirements to the property
    groups without taking ownership of their internal domain meanings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="interoperability">Interoperability Working Group</h2>
  <p>
    Interoperability is a peer of the domain and scheme groups, not a child of one group.
    Representatives agree only the boundary arrangements needed for exchange: a small
    common boundary, a context map, qualified mappings, and shared identifier, provenance,
    versioning and change conventions.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/working-groups/join">Find participation routes and joining information</a>.</p>
</Layout>
